[b]Disclaimer: this mod was made with AI assistance.[/b] If you're not comfortable with that, please stop reading here.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/banner.jpg[/img]

Homemade 1993 electric vehicles for [b]Dazed Power[/b] on [b]Build 42[/b]. Convert a small car, pickup or van to electric, rebuild a golf cart, or build a little wedge car on a scrapped frame. Fill the pack with car batteries, makeshift batteries or heavy deep-cycle batteries, and charge it from your wired Dazed Power system. This is an [b]early test build[/b]: the first vehicles work, and much more is planned.

[table]
[tr][td][b]Game version[/b][/td][td]Build 42 only (42.0+)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Requires[/b][/td][td][b]Dazed Core[/b] and [b]Dazed Power[/b] (subscribe to both)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Multiplayer[/b][/td][td]Built for it, server is the authority. Early build, reports welcome[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Add mid-save[/b][/td][td]Yes. Club carts and Elec-Traks only spawn in parts of the map not yet explored[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Status[/b][/td][td]Test build, version 0.1.0[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Mod ID[/b][/td][td]DazedPowerEV[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-build.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/vehicles.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Garage Conversion[/b]: seven donor cars, liveries included: Chevalier Dart, Masterson Horizon, Chevalier D6, Franklin Valuline, Chevalier Nyala, Dash Rancher and Chevalier Cerise Wagon. 10 battery slots, 120 V. It runs at about three quarters of the donor's speed and power.
[*][b]Club Cart[/b]: 36 V golf cart, 3 battery slots, 22 km/h, two seats. Found in well-off neighbourhoods, trailer parks and farms with a few tired batteries, or built from parts.
[*][b]Elec-Trak[/b]: 36 V garden tractor, 3 battery slots, 11 km/h, one seat. Found on farms, in trailer parks and junkyards.
[*][b]Wedge car[/b]: a homemade CitiCar-style two-seater, 48 V, 4 battery slots, 60 km/h. Only built, never found.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-building.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/building.png[/img]
[list]
[*][i]Convert It![/i] teaches the conversion. Right-click a donor car from outside: [b]Convert to electric[/b]. Needs Mechanics 5, Electrical 5, Metalworking 3, a rewound traction motor, a homemade motor controller, wire, sheet metal and screws. The old engine comes back as engine parts and scrap.
[*][i]Golf Cart Rebuild[/i] teaches the cart, its motor and a resistor-coil controller. Right-click clear ground: [b]Build club cart here[/b]. Needs Mechanics 2 and Electrical 2.
[*][i]Build Your Own Commuter Car[/i] teaches the wedge car. Empty a Chevalier Dart or Masterson Horizon and right-click it: [b]Build a wedge car on this frame[/b]. Needs Mechanics 4, Electrical 4, and Metalworking 3 or Carpentry 3.
[*]Built vehicles roll out with an empty battery tray.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-pack.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/pack.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Car batteries[/b] hold 720 Wh. [b]Makeshift car batteries[/b] (12 torch batteries in a box, Electrical 2) hold 240 Wh and wear out fast. [b]Heavy deep-cycle batteries[/b] hold 1,400 Wh and last about three times as long as a car battery.
[*]Mix them freely. Install and remove them from the vehicle's [b]Battery pack[/b] menu; each keeps its own charge and condition.
[*]Batteries wear with use. Heavy batteries cut power and top speed.
[*]Deep-cycle batteries turn up in barns, farm crates, golf stores, army surplus, camping, hardware and car supply stores.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-driving.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/driving.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Driving uses charge by distance, more flat out. Headlights, heater and radio draw from the pack too.
[*]Cold weather cuts range, using Dazed Power's battery cold factor.
[*]Below 15% the vehicle limps at half power and half speed, below 5% it crawls, and a flat pack stalls it.
[*]The fuel gauge reads the pack, and a Dazed Power-style dashboard shows charge, motor power, volts, range and the batteries, with LIMP, LOW, PLUG and COLD lamps.
[*]Electric vehicles are quiet. Gas cans and pumps don't work on them.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-charging.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/charging.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Park and [b]Plug in charging lead[/b] to the nearest wired Dazed Power part within 10 tiles. It charges at 600 W from your battery banks, above the discharge floor. Driving off pulls the lead.
[*]Dazed Power's charging bench also charges makeshift and deep-cycle batteries, so you can keep a spare set ready and swap.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-planned.png[/img]
Planned for later: a graded EV charger part with its own light and hum, a motor whine, rear seats giving way to batteries in four-seaters, makeshift batteries in Dazed Power's banks, pack heat and failures, Elec-Trak tools and trailer, a ride-on, trailers, roof solar and a guide page. Plans can change.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-compat.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Build 42 only. Needs [b]Dazed Power[/b] for charging, its battery maths and its dashboard look.
[*]Vanilla vehicles only for conversion. Burnt and smashed wrecks can't be converted.
[*]No sandbox options yet.
[*]This is a test build. Expect rough edges, and back up your save before trying it.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-help.png[/img]
Post in the Discussions tab. Include your game version, the Dazed mods you run, which vehicle, and your console.txt if there is an error.

